{
  "raw": {
    "https://willamette.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Portland-Campus/PNCA-Dean-of-Students-for-Community-Care---Inclusion_R0007285": {
      "title": "PNCA Dean of Students for Community Care & Inclusion",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT WILLAMETTE UNIVERSITY: Willamette University , founded in 1842, is a nationally-renowned private university enrolling 2800 students across five colleges. Our historic campus, adjacent to the Oregon State Capitol, hosts a distinguished undergraduate liberal arts college in Salem, Oregon. Our downtown Portland campus is home to the Pacific Northwest College of Art (PNCA). We offer a wide range of professional graduate programs, including Oregon’s top-ranked MBA program , the Northwest’s oldest law school, as well as MA/MFA programs at PNCA and master’s degrees in data science and computer science. Willamette University provides a high-value and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our Benefits Summary includes options for health, dental, life insurance, retirement, substantial paid time off, tuition and more. If you need assistance applying for a job or have any questions on recruitment at Willamette, please contact our HR Department , hr@willamette.edu or call us at 503-370-6210. POSITION SUMMARY Reporting to the Vice President of Student Affairs at Willamette University in Salem, the Dean of Students for Community Care and Inclusion serves as the senior student affairs administrator  and primary manager for the Office of Student Affairs at the Pacific Northwest College of the Arts (PNCA) in Portland, with approximately 400 undergraduate and 100 graduate students, with 100 primarily first-year students reside in apartment-style living in “ArtHouse”.The Dean collaborates with campus partners across the College and the larger University community to create environments and initiatives that support students’ sense of belonging, wellbeing, and engagement that fosters students’ success. The Dean serves as the supervisor for 2 professional staff members: the Assistant Director of Student Affairs who also serves as the live-in professional for ArtHouse, and the Director of Community Care and Health Education. The Dean oversees the advocacy and support efforts for students experiencing distress through the student CARE process that includes a multidisciplinary team that works to assist students in need of personal care and/or academic resources. The Dean also oversees the student code of conduct at PNCA which ensures the fair and equitable management of the student conduct process and student conflict resolution initiatives, and serves as a Deputy Title IX Coordinator. The Dean ensures appropriate oversight for student events, student clubs and organization advising, and student engagement and coordinates new student orientation. The Dean serves in an on-call rotation to support on-call RAs and Campus Safety Officers and for emergency response. The Dean of Students leads efforts to ensure the PNCA Student Affairs department fosters a welcoming campus environment, and aligns with divisional, college, and university policies and goals. The Dean serves as a relationship builder--mentoring, advising, and connecting with students and members of the campus community to identify needs and develop strategies to enhance the student experience at PNCA. The Dean collaborates with the Academic Dean, Campus Security, facilities, faculty, and staff on the PNCA and Salem campuses in accomplishing these goals. RESPONSIBILITIES   General Management Responsibilities Serve as a strategic thought leader who integrates an understanding of student development, wellbeing, cultural fluency, and crisis management in the implementation of initiatives that support student success and thriving communities. Assist in creating and fostering a culture of personal growth and development for Student Affairs staff; provides adequate training and supervision to support supervisees in carrying out their responsibilities and implementing changes to service models, staffing, outreach and other areas in response to evolving student needs. Provide innovative and strategic leadership for the programmatic and operational functions of the Office of Student Affairs at PNCA. Ensure day-to-day operations include efficient systems to meet professional standards and timely and sensitive response to students', families', and University community members' questions, concerns, and requests for assistance. Work with direct reports to ensure effective and responsible stewardship of finances and resources. Maintain an accessible and visible campus presence; is available for relevant  university events, staff/student-planned community development activities, and emergency response. Management of student conduct and conflict resolution processes Oversee the PNCA student conduct process which includes case distribution, investigations, adjudications, sanctioning and overall management of student conduct. Ensures the student conduct process is administered in a fair, impartial, non-adversarial, restorative, and educational manner and that staff involved in the process are trained appropriately. Ensure staff’s timely follow up to violations of residence hall and University policies. Oversee the direction, training, advising, and facilitation of effective conflict resolution involving students. Coordinate and facilitate dispute resolution processes as needed. Serve as an Administrative/University Hearing Officer, investigator, or member of the University conduct panel hearing board for high level judicial and Title IX cases as needed. Lead efforts to educate the University community on policies, procedures, and/or resources pertaining to student conduct/behavioral expectations and supporting students in distress. Collaborate with the Academic Dean and faculty on student behavior concerns. ​Management of student care and case management processes Serve as the Chairperson for the CARE Team. Work closely with the Director of Community Care and Health Education to prepare meeting agendas, and ensure team input, case assignments and timely follow up. Work with the AVP/Dean of Students and Assistant Dean for Community Care & Inclusion in Salem to establish CARE Team protocols and training to CARE team members and community as needed. Monitor communication/outreach efforts to students. Oversee PNCA crisis management response and protocols for supporting students in distress; work collaboratively with PNCA faculty and staff and Salem campus staff as needed. In collaboration with the Associate Dean for Health and Wellbeing, oversees post- hospitalization support to students returning from a mental/behavioral health setting and transitioning back to the University environment. New Student and Family Orientation Lead the development and coordination of the new student and family orientation program in collaboration with direct reports, the Academic Dean, and appropriate faculty. Create the new student and family orientation communication plan (e.g., website, e-mails, social media) with campus partners. Coordinate opening logistics with campus partners. Student Engagement Establish goals and priorities for student engagement. Ensure programs/initiatives promote students’ sense of belonging, community development, and overall well-being. Ensure the on-going development of initiatives in partnership with faculty and staff based on community interests and student needs. Ensure the development of the Student Council and solicit feedback from members of the student council on the creation of policies, initiatives, and programs. Meet regularly with student leaders. Ensure a clear club registration process and orientation and training for student leaders. Ensure fiscal guidance and ethical use for student activities fund usage and expenditures. Maintains visibility through on-campus presence, attending events and engaging in appropriate outreach to develop and maintain relationships with students, faculty, and staff. Divisional Leadership Attend divisional meetings and trainings. Chaperone and assist in organization of large, campus-wide programs as needed such as orientation events, accepted students days, First Thursdays and commencement. Assist in leading task forces, presenting training topics, and executing divisional and university projects as needed. QUALIFICATIONS Minimum A Master's degree in Student Personnel, Counseling, or related discipline is required Strong writing and presentation skills Ability to implement problem solving strategies to manage everyday challenges such as crisis response, conflict management, community development, student activism, and student/family concerns in a fast-paced environment. Can function competently under pressure and effectively diffuses crisis situations to demonstrate sound judgment Supervision experience Experience in higher education or student affairs ​ Preferred Preferred candidates have at least 10 years of progressive student affairs experience in crisis management, student care, advising, supervision, student conduct, and program planning. Previous experience at a college of art is preferred. Possess a sound background in student/human development theory, Title IX, student mental health, crisis management, supervision, community development and student success. Knowledge of relevant laws such as Title IX, Clery Act, Campus Sexual Violence prevention (Campus SaVE) Act, Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA), the ADA Involvement in local, regional, and national organizations supporting the field of student affairs (such as ACPA and NASPA). Typical Work Schedule: In-person work 8 am to 5 pm, remote work only when students are not in session; participate in on-call rotation Physical Demands & Working Conditions: Typical work is performed indoors in a normal office environment. Salary: $100,000-115,000 Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis as received until position is filled. You will need to upload the following two documents as part of your application materials in the \"My Experience\" section labeled Resume: Cover letter addressing the required/desired qualifications and presenting any other applicant characteristics which deserve emphasis Current Resume ​ Incomplete applications will not be considered. BACKGROUND CHECK REQUIREMENT: All University positions require that candidates submit to a criminal conviction record check prior to hire. Conviction does not automatically preclude candidates from being hired. Nature of conviction will be considered relative to the duties of the position.   REASONABLE ACCOMMODATIONS STATEMENT: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. INSTRUCTIONS FOR APPLICANTS: Please read the following carefully before beginning the online application process. To be considered for employment at Willamette University, please complete our online employment application. Your application and all required attachments -- listed at the bottom of the page -- must be submitted for each individual job post that you are interested in applying. Once you submit your application you will not be able to edit your application."
    },
    "https://willamette.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Portland-Campus/Assistant-Director-of-Student-Affairs--PNCA_R0007233": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Student Affairs, PNCA",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT WILLAMETTE UNIVERSITY: Willamette University , founded in 1842, is a nationally-renowned private university enrolling 2800 students across five colleges. Our historic campus, adjacent to the Oregon State Capitol, hosts a distinguished undergraduate liberal arts college in Salem, Oregon. Our downtown Portland campus is home to the Pacific Northwest College of Art (PNCA). We offer a wide range of professional graduate programs, including Oregon’s top-ranked MBA program , the Northwest’s oldest law school, as well as MA/MFA programs at PNCA and master’s degrees in data science and computer science. Willamette University provides a high-value and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our Benefits Summary includes options for health, dental, life insurance, retirement, substantial paid time off, tuition and more. If you need assistance applying for a job or have any questions on recruitment at Willamette, please contact our HR Department , hr@willamette.edu or call us at 503-370-6210. POSITION SUMMARY Reporting to the Dean of Students for Community Care & Inclusion, the Assistant Director of Student Affairs assists in overseeing the co-curricular engagement of 400 undergraduate students and 40 graduate students. In collaboration with the PNCA Student Affairs team, the Assistant Director’s responsibilities are aimed at creating inclusive environments, events, and initiatives that support students’ sense of belonging, holistic learning, well-being, leadership development, and engagement that fosters students’ success. In close coordination with the Residential Life and Housing team on Willamette University’s Salem Campus, the Assistant Director assumes responsibility for the operation of ArtHouse, an apartment-style residential facility in downtown Portland that houses 130 first-year students and includes the supervision of 4-6 Resident Assistants. This is a live-in position and requires some evening and weekend availability. The Assistant Director serves as a University conduct officer and is a member of the Student Care Team, ensuring case management support and assistance to students in crisis and distress and serving in an on-call rotation for emergency and response. RESPONSIBILITIES Engagement & Community Development Advise and support recognized undergraduate and graduate student organizations and Arthouse Hall Council; meet regularly with their executive teams. Oversee student leaders in planning and implementing events. Lead and/or assist in the program planning and implementation of campus-wide events and initiatives such as New Student and Family Orientation, Family Weekend, Holiday Art Fair, Cultural Heritage Months, other affinity-based programming, personal development opportunities, and social events & programs. Develop community-building and educational initiatives based on the Student Affairs Division curriculum and PNCA goals that support student learning, engagement, and belonging. Develop and support student recognition initiatives and promote leadership opportunities. Allocate and maintain student lockers. Maintain visibility, engage regularly with students, and attend campus and community programs. Provide budgetary oversight to assigned budget accounts. Ensure compliance with institutional budget policies. Arthouse Facilities Operations & Residence Life Assist in overall administration of the residence life and housing program. Coordinate facility management, housing operations, and communication with residents with PTLA property management group. Assist in the development and evaluation of housing policies, procedures, and goals. Educate RAs and residents on safety and security concerns and appropriate emergency response procedures. Assumes other duties as assigned by the Director of Residential Life and Housing and Dean of Students for Community Care & Inclusion Recruit, train, and supervise 4-6 Resident Advisors and Office of Student Affairs student employees. Provide ongoing feedback and support to student staff. Oversees RA responsibilities in the communication of community expectations of students and response to behavioral issues. Establish a sense of teamwork and collaboration among RAs. Provide team-building opportunities to promote good RA relations. ​Student CARE, Conduct, and Conflict Resolution Serve as a Conduct Hearing officer.  Investigate incidents, facilitate Administrative Hearings, determine responsibility, assign sanctions as appropriate, make appropriate referrals, and write related conduct letters. Mediate conflicts between students, facilitating discussions to resolve disputes and promote an inclusive and supportive living environment. Support students in distress and help facilitate student wellbeing Serve as a member of the CARE team, responding to CARE Reports as a case manager to provide support to students experiencing difficulties. Crisis Response and Management Serve in a scheduled on-call rotation to respond to student emergencies and crises, providing immediate support and intervention. QUALIFICATIONS Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Two years experience working in residence life on a university campus. Demonstrated experience organizing events and programs. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Demonstrated experience and comfortability with providing support to students in distress, mental health challenges, and interpersonal conflict Evidence of cultural sensitivity and competence for effectively engaging and working within a culturally diverse community Preferred Qualifications Masters Degree in college student personnel, higher education leadership, social work, psychology or related field. Experience coordinating and/or organizing projects and programs in a diverse environment within higher education, preferably experience working with art students Experience responding to and working with diverse, at-risk, disadvantaged, and historically underrepresented student populations. Demonstrated experience implementing best practices and strategies in student engagement, development, persistence retention, campus services, leadership development, and student success. Experience working at an art and design college Excellent multi-project organizational management skills. Experience providing support to students experiencing academic challenges, mental health concerns, roommate conflicts, and personal concerns. Experience responding to crisis and/or early intervention (i.e., on-call for emergency response, conflict mediation, responding to medical or mental health emergencies, fire alarms, etc.). Typical Work Schedule Monday through Friday, 8 am to 5 pm Evening and weekend hours as needed and are common This position also serves on a scheduled on-call rotation Physical Demands & Working Conditions: Typical work is performed indoors in a normal office environment. Salary: $54,654 annually You will need to upload the following documents as part of your application materials in the \"My Experience\" section labeled Resume: Cover letter addressing the required/desired qualifications and presenting any other applicant characteristics which deserve emphasis Current resume   Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis as received until the position is filled.   Incomplete applications will not be considered.  BACKGROUND CHECK REQUIREMENT: All University positions require that candidates submit to a criminal conviction record check prior to hire. Conviction does not automatically preclude candidates from being hired. Nature of conviction will be considered relative to the duties of the position.   REASONABLE ACCOMMODATIONS STATEMENT: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. INSTRUCTIONS FOR APPLICANTS: Please read the following carefully before beginning the online application process. To be considered for employment at Willamette University, please complete our online employment application. Your application and all required attachments -- listed at the bottom of the page -- must be submitted for each individual job post that you are interested in applying. Once you submit your application you will not be able to edit your application."
    },
    "https://willamette.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Salem-Campus/Instructional-Technology-Associate_R0007141": {
      "title": "Instructional Technology Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nABOUT WILLAMETTE UNIVERSITY: Willamette University , founded in 1842, is a nationally-renowned private university enrolling 2800 students across five colleges. Our historic campus, adjacent to the Oregon State Capitol, hosts a distinguished undergraduate liberal arts college in Salem, Oregon. Our downtown Portland campus is home to the Pacific Northwest College of Art (PNCA). We offer a wide range of professional graduate programs, including Oregon’s top-ranked MBA program , the Northwest’s oldest law school, as well as MA/MFA programs at PNCA and master’s degrees in data science and computer science. Willamette University provides a high-value and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our Benefits Summary includes options for health, dental, life insurance, retirement, substantial paid time off, tuition and more. If you need assistance applying for a job or have any questions on recruitment at Willamette, please contact our HR Department , hr@willamette.edu or call us at 503-370-6210. POSITION SUMMARY The Instructional Technology Associate is a collaborative role within Willamette University Information Technology (WITS) division, and is responsible for supporting and advancing the University’s Learning Management System and broader instructional technology environment. This position partners closely with stakeholders to promote accessibility and best practices of academic technologies across online and hybrid learning environments. This role serves as a key resource for LMS support, and a collaborative resource for emerging educational technologies including responsible applications of artificial intelligence in teaching and learning. The position works closely with Academic Technology and campus partners to enhance the overall digital learning experience for students and faculty. RESPONSIBILITIES Learning Management System Support: Serve as a technical resource for the University’s learning   management system (Canvas), supporting course delivery and effective use of LMS features and   integrations. LMS End User Support: Serve as primary triage and escalation for all support requests related to   learning management and related systems. Academic Technology Support: Support instructional technologies used in course delivery and academic   engagement (including AI-enabled tools and LTI’s in our Learning Management System). Collaboration and Coordination: Collaborate with Academic Technology, WITS teams, faculty and   campus stakeholders to support optimization of the Learning Management System. Accessibility and Usability: Support accessibility best practices and promote inclusive design principles   within digital learning environments. Assist with projects as delegated related to documentation and support resources to strengthen   institutional use of instructional technologies. Additional Duties: Perform other related duties as assigned in support of evolving academic technology   and instructional needs. QUALIFICATIONS Minimum : Bachelor’s degree preferred in a related field, or equivalent professional experience. Preferred Experience supporting learning management systems such as Canvas or similar platforms. Experience supporting instructional technology within higher education or a comparable environment. Excellent communication, collaboration, and relationship-building skills with the ability to translate technical concepts into practical guidance. Strong organizational and project coordination skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities effectively. Understanding of accessibility and usability best practices within digital learning environments. Interest in emerging educational technologies, including responsible applications of artificial intelligence in higher education. Typical Work Schedule: Part-time, 20 hours per week. Schedule is flexible but must provide regular availability between 8:00 a.m. and 5:00 p.m., Monday through Friday, based on departmental needs. ​ Physical Demands & Working Conditions: Ability to perform work in a standard office environment, including prolonged periods of sitting and computer use. Must be able to occasionally move equipment weighing up to 25 pounds and travel between campus locations as needed. Salary: $40-45/hour, depending on experience You will need to upload the following two documents as part of your application materials in the \"My Experience\" section labeled Resume: Cover letter addressing qualifications Current resume Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. ​Incomplete applications will not be considered. Typical work schedule BACKGROUND CHECK REQUIREMENT: All University positions require that candidates submit to a criminal conviction record check prior to hire. Conviction does not automatically preclude candidates from being hired. Nature of conviction will be considered relative to the duties of the position.   REASONABLE ACCOMMODATIONS STATEMENT: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. INSTRUCTIONS FOR APPLICANTS: Please read the following carefully before beginning the online application process. To be considered for employment at Willamette University, please complete our online employment application. Your application and all required attachments -- listed at the bottom of the page -- must be submitted for each individual job post that you are interested in applying. Once you submit your application you will not be able to edit your application."
    },
    "https://willamette.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Portland-Campus/Life-Model_R0007148": {
      "title": "Life Model",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nABOUT WILLAMETTE UNIVERSITY: Willamette University , founded in 1842, is a nationally-renowned private university enrolling 2800 students across five colleges. Our historic campus, adjacent to the Oregon State Capitol, hosts a distinguished undergraduate liberal arts college in Salem, Oregon. Our downtown Portland campus is home to the Pacific Northwest College of Art (PNCA). We offer a wide range of professional graduate programs, including Oregon’s top-ranked MBA program , the Northwest’s oldest law school, as well as MA/MFA programs at PNCA and master’s degrees in data science and computer science. Willamette University provides a high-value and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our Benefits Summary includes options for health, dental, life insurance, retirement, substantial paid time off, tuition and more. If you need assistance applying for a job or have any questions on recruitment at Willamette, please contact our HR Department , hr@willamette.edu or call us at 503-370-6210. POSITION SUMMARY The Life Model serves as a model for a variety of courses at Pacific Northwest College of Art (PNCA). This position is part time with flexible scheduling. We encourage all ages and body types to apply. The Life Model supports a diverse range of classes which include: Drawing, Painting, Illustration, Sculpture, 3D Design, and Animation. Life Models are an integral part of PNCA. Models give students the opportunity to work from life and gain valuable skills in observation, proportion, gesture, form, volume, movement, structure, and composition. As a Life Model, you will provide dynamic and inspiring poses for art students and professional artists. Your role will be pivotal in the creative process, offering a range of poses to support various artistic styles and mediums. Pacific Northwest College of Art is actively recruiting for a wide range of ethnicities, body types, age, abilities, etc. RESPONSIBILITIES Sustains a variety of nude or clothed poses for art students during classes up to 3 hours in duration. Clothed sessions may include: costumed, street wear, drapery or athletic clothing. Provides a full range of traditional life drawing poses, from gestures to sustained poses, as required by tradition and as directed by the instructor Poses in person Maintains personal space and life modeling etiquette. Observes standard life model practices (i.e., brings own robe to wear between poses, etc.) QUALIFICATIONS Minimum Comfortable being nude or clothed in front of 20 or more artists for the duration of the pose Ability to appropriately, sensitively, and professionally interact with instructors and students Ability to work a flexible schedule including evenings as needed Ability to keep scheduled commitments and be on time for modeling Models of all ages and all body types are encouraged to apply Preferred Experience with yoga or dance poses Prior modeling experience Typical Work Schedule: 9 hours of modeling per month Physical Demands & Working Conditions: Must be able to hold standing or seated poses for a minimum of 20 minutes. Accommodations can be made as needed. Salary: $20.81/hour You will need to upload the following two documents as part of your application materials in the \"My Experience\" section labeled Resume: Cover letter addressing qualifications Current resume Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. Hiring for fall positions and scheduling will begin no later than August 1, 2026. ​Incomplete applications will not be considered. BACKGROUND CHECK REQUIREMENT: All University positions require that candidates submit to a criminal conviction record check prior to hire. Conviction does not automatically preclude candidates from being hired. Nature of conviction will be considered relative to the duties of the position.   REASONABLE ACCOMMODATIONS STATEMENT: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. INSTRUCTIONS FOR APPLICANTS: Please read the following carefully before beginning the online application process. To be considered for employment at Willamette University, please complete our online employment application. Your application and all required attachments -- listed at the bottom of the page -- must be submitted for each individual job post that you are interested in applying. Once you submit your application you will not be able to edit your application."
    },
    "https://willamette.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Portland-Campus/PNCA-Student-Affairs-Office-Assistant_R0007140": {
      "title": "PNCA Student Affairs Office Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nABOUT WILLAMETTE UNIVERSITY: Willamette University , founded in 1842, is a nationally-renowned private university enrolling 2800 students across five colleges. Our historic campus, adjacent to the Oregon State Capitol, hosts a distinguished undergraduate liberal arts college in Salem, Oregon. Our downtown Portland campus is home to the Pacific Northwest College of Art (PNCA). We offer a wide range of professional graduate programs, including Oregon’s top-ranked MBA program , the Northwest’s oldest law school, as well as MA/MFA programs at PNCA and master’s degrees in data science and computer science. Willamette University provides a high-value and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our Benefits Summary includes options for health, dental, life insurance, retirement, substantial paid time off, tuition and more. If you need assistance applying for a job or have any questions on recruitment at Willamette, please contact our HR Department , hr@willamette.edu or call us at 503-370-6210. POSITION SUMMARY Reporting to the Dean of Students for Community Care & Inclusion at PNCA, the Student Affairs Office Assistant plays a critical role in providing comprehensive administrative support and operational coordination for the PNCA Office of Student Affairs. This role assists student clubs and organizations, provides support for key campus events, office coverage, marketing, and promotion for departmental events. This position will participate in major university-wide events, including admitted student days, orientation, move-in, and admissions events. RESPONSIBILITIES Student Engagement and Leadership Support Act as the primary point of contact for active undergraduate and graduate student clubs and organizations, helping them navigate university processes. Assist active student clubs and organizations with purchasing items approved by the Student Council (graduate and undergraduate) Supervise the work of student office assistants Administrative Support & Office Operations Manage email and communication requests from active clubs and organizations at PNCA and the general pnca-student-life@willamette.edu account, routing to the appropriate staff member or responding accordingly. Assist with reconciliation of monthly expenditures of the PNCA Student Affairs Team (DOS, Director, & Assistant Director) Provide coverage for the Office of Student Affairs, PNCA Provide Office support, including tracking and monitoring of supplies, general office organization, and maintenance (watering plants, tidying the office, organizing student affairs supplies) Assist the Office with scheduling and coordinating meetings with external constituents and campus partners. Manage Student Life marketing and promotions. Event Coordination & Marketing Provide general support for key campus activities and events, which can include assistance with purchasing, set-up, breakdown, and other duties. Assist with flyer and poster design for the Office of Student Affairs Actively participate in major University events such as Orientation, Move-in, Move-out, Admitted Students Day, and Admissions events. Professionalism & Compliance Respect and maintain confidentiality, parameters of operation, professional protocols, and individual privacy as required by law. Perform other duties as assigned by supervisor or their designee. QUALIFICATIONS Minimum High School Diploma. Ability to cultivate relationships with campus constituents. Ability to effectively communicate with diverse audiences. Understanding of event planning processes and ability to support student groups in executing successful events. Ability to provide administrative support to functional areas in a timely manner. Preferred Bachelor's Degree from an accredited higher education institution Familiarity with an art and design college environment Previous experience working with college students Previous experience working in an office environment Experience using Google Applications, Canva, Adobe, or other products to design flyers. Typical Work Schedule: Monday through Thursday, 9:00 am to 2:00 pm. Occasional Fridays and evenings. Physical Demands & Working Conditions: Typical work is performed indoors in a normal office environment. Salary: $18.95/hr for an average of 20 hours a week. You will need to upload the following two documents as part of your application materials in the \"My Experience\" section labeled Resume: Cover letter addressing qualifications Current resume Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. ​Incomplete applications will not be considered. BACKGROUND CHECK REQUIREMENT: All University positions require that candidates submit to a criminal conviction record check prior to hire. Conviction does not automatically preclude candidates from being hired. Nature of conviction will be considered relative to the duties of the position.   REASONABLE ACCOMMODATIONS STATEMENT: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. INSTRUCTIONS FOR APPLICANTS: Please read the following carefully before beginning the online application process. To be considered for employment at Willamette University, please complete our online employment application. Your application and all required attachments -- listed at the bottom of the page -- must be submitted for each individual job post that you are interested in applying. Once you submit your application you will not be able to edit your application."
    },
    "https://willamette.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Salem-Campus/Artist-Associate_R0007126": {
      "title": "Artist Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nABOUT WILLAMETTE UNIVERSITY: Willamette University , founded in 1842, is a nationally-renowned private university enrolling 2800 students across five colleges. Our historic campus, adjacent to the Oregon State Capitol, hosts a distinguished undergraduate liberal arts college in Salem, Oregon. Our downtown Portland campus is home to the Pacific Northwest College of Art (PNCA). We offer a wide range of professional graduate programs, including Oregon’s top-ranked MBA program , the Northwest’s oldest law school, as well as MA/MFA programs at PNCA and master’s degrees in data science and computer science. Willamette University provides a high-value and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our Benefits Summary includes options for health, dental, life insurance, retirement, substantial paid time off, tuition and more. If you need assistance applying for a job or have any questions on recruitment at Willamette, please contact our HR Department , hr@willamette.edu or call us at 503-370-6210. POSITION SUMMARY Willamette University seeks a pool of qualified music lesson instructors in the areas of trumpet, percussion, piano, and voice. Duties include weekly private instruction plus opportunities to coach small ensembles in area(s) of expertise, coordinate large ensemble sectionals, teach academic music courses as needed and according to background, as well as collaborate professionally with faculty and students in departmental musical offerings. RESPONSIBILITIES Provide up to 15 hours of lessons or other assignments per week, for a 14-week semester for a maximum 210 hours per semester. Other remunerated hourly assignments, offered based on departmental need and in consultation with the Department Chair, may include recital and performance juries, assisting with auditions, chamber music and jazz combo coaching, ensemble conducting, and other collaborative performance opportunities. QUALIFICATIONS Minimum: Outstanding and active performer with evidence of successful teaching experience and a strong desire to motivate and see students succeed. Preferred: Advanced degree in Music. Typical Work Schedule: Lessons take place Monday through Friday based on student/instructor availability. Physical Demands & Working Conditions: Typical work is performed indoors in a normal office environment. Salary: $62.43/hour You will need to upload the following two documents as part of your application materials in the \"My Experience\" section labeled Resume: Cover letter addressing qualifications Current resume Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. ​Incomplete applications will not be considered. BACKGROUND CHECK REQUIREMENT: All University positions require that candidates submit to a criminal conviction record check prior to hire. Conviction does not automatically preclude candidates from being hired. Nature of conviction will be considered relative to the duties of the position.   REASONABLE ACCOMMODATIONS STATEMENT: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. INSTRUCTIONS FOR APPLICANTS: Please read the following carefully before beginning the online application process. To be considered for employment at Willamette University, please complete our online employment application. Your application and all required attachments -- listed at the bottom of the page -- must be submitted for each individual job post that you are interested in applying. Once you submit your application you will not be able to edit your application."
    },
    "https://willamette.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Portland-Campus/Campus-Safety-Officer_R0007125": {
      "title": "Campus Safety Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT WILLAMETTE UNIVERSITY: Willamette University , founded in 1842, is a nationally-renowned private university enrolling 2800 students across five colleges. Our historic campus, adjacent to the Oregon State Capitol, hosts a distinguished undergraduate liberal arts college in Salem, Oregon. Our downtown Portland campus is home to the Pacific Northwest College of Art (PNCA). We offer a wide range of professional graduate programs, including Oregon’s top-ranked MBA program , the Northwest’s oldest law school, as well as MA/MFA programs at PNCA and master’s degrees in data science and computer science. Willamette University provides a high-value and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our Benefits Summary includes options for health, dental, life insurance, retirement, substantial paid time off, tuition and more. If you need assistance applying for a job or have any questions on recruitment at Willamette, please contact our HR Department , hr@willamette.edu or call us at 503-370-6210. POSITION SUMMARY Campus Safety Officers are responsible for helping ensure the safety and security of Willamette University's students, employees, visitors, and property during their assigned shifts. They deal with all violations of law and campus policy in an appropriate and equitable manner and positively engage with diverse individuals and groups in support of an inclusive environment. The Campus Safety Officer position reports to the Associate Director of Campus Safety. This position is responsible for responding to situations utilizing a set of well-defined policies, procedures, and expectations. Must be able to perform duties with independence. Provides direction and supervision to work-study students but has no formal responsibility for supervision. Public relations are an important part of this position. Requires strong interpersonal and verbal communication skills to exchange information with individuals both inside and outside the University. Requires an understanding of a culturally diverse community and the need to interact in a manner that fosters positive relationships in respectful, equitable, and inclusive ways.   Duties and Responsibilities Campus Safety Officers are responsible for helping ensure the safety and security of Willamette University's students, employees, visitors, and property during their assigned shifts. Patrol university grounds and facilities to ensure a safe and secure environment, including on foot and in vehicles, patrol campus facilities, parking lots, grounds, and the interior of all buildings on campus. Monitor all activity and confront any suspicious behavior on Campus. Escort visitors and intruders off campus if required. Issue citations and warnings to violators. Interview individuals involved in incidents, gather information and write reports on crimes, violence, vandalism, fires, and other illegal activities on campus. Give accounts of people involved, who are affected, and what measures were taken to minimize or eliminate the incidents. Respond quickly to all calls to Campus Safety for assistance and contact local Police, Fire, or Medical personnel when necessary. Provides medical care at the basic first aid/CPR/AED level as provided by the American Red Cross or its equivalent. Coordinates with medical responders when a higher level of care is required. Responds to notifications from the security and fire alarms across campus that are monitored by campus Safety. Contribute to the support and implementation of the University Strategic Plan. Adhere to University policies and procedures. Updates daily activity logs as needed and in a timely manner; completes written incident and investigative reports in a timely, clear, and well-written manner. Perform other duties as assigned.   Minimum Qualifications Must meet minimum qualifications for certification standards set by the Department of Public Safety Standards and Training (DPSST). DPSST requires candidates to be a minimum of 18 years of age to obtain an Unarmed Private Security certification. High school diploma or GED Minimum of two years experience in a security position or two years of college-level law enforcement or criminal justice courses And/ Or any combination of education and experience that provides the required knowledge, skills, and abilities to perform the position's essential functions. Ability to operate a computer, with demonstrated skills in Outlook, Word, Excel, and other security-related programs.  Valid driver’s license within 60 days of hire. CPR/AED Certification or obtain within 90 days of employment. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills are necessary, as well as the ability to actively communicate with various constituents, including faculty, staff, administration, and the general public. Demonstrated ability to efficiently and effectively solve problems and initiate and implement projects independently. Ability to multi-task with accuracy and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Experience working with diverse populations. Preferred Qualifications Customer service experience. Experience working in a security-related field. Experience working at a college or university. Physical Demands and Working Conditions Typical schedule requires 40 hour per work with possible required overtime as needed Requires standing for long periods of time and taking many stairs/runs as part of your regular patrol duties.  Requires to kneel/crawl, twist, lift, carry, push, and pull objects that weigh up to 50 pounds. Salary: $23.93/ hour   You will need to upload the following document as part of your application materials in the \"My Experience\" section labeled Resume: Current Resume   Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis as received until the position is filled.   Incomplete applications will not be considered.  BACKGROUND CHECK REQUIREMENT: All University positions require that candidates submit to a criminal conviction record check prior to hire. Conviction does not automatically preclude candidates from being hired. Nature of conviction will be considered relative to the duties of the position.   REASONABLE ACCOMMODATIONS STATEMENT: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. INSTRUCTIONS FOR APPLICANTS: Please read the following carefully before beginning the online application process. To be considered for employment at Willamette University, please complete our online employment application. Your application and all required attachments -- listed at the bottom of the page -- must be submitted for each individual job post that you are interested in applying. Once you submit your application you will not be able to edit your application."
    },
    "https://willamette.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Salem-Campus/Assistant-Coach--Football--Part-Time-_R0007028": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Football (Part Time)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nABOUT WILLAMETTE UNIVERSITY: Willamette University , founded in 1842, is a nationally-renowned private university enrolling 2800 students across five colleges. Our historic campus, adjacent to the Oregon State Capitol, hosts a distinguished undergraduate liberal arts college in Salem, Oregon. Our downtown Portland campus is home to the Pacific Northwest College of Art (PNCA). We offer a wide range of professional graduate programs, including Oregon’s top-ranked MBA program , the Northwest’s oldest law school, as well as MA/MFA programs at PNCA and master’s degrees in data science and computer science. Willamette University provides a high-value and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our Benefits Summary includes options for health, dental, life insurance, retirement, substantial paid time off, tuition and more. If you need assistance applying for a job or have any questions on recruitment at Willamette, please contact our HR Department , hr@willamette.edu or call us at 503-370-6210. POSITION SUMMARY Willamette Football seeks two part-time Assistant Coaches for defensive backs and wide receivers. Assistant coaches will assist the Head Coach in all aspects of running a football program. The assistant coaches will help coach workouts, practices, and competitions, and work with player development. RESPONSIBILITIES Instruct, teach, and coach student-athletes during practices and competition Conduct video analysis of games and practice that will be used for teaching and preparation Work with staff members on the game plan Identify and recruit potential team members Retain current team members Responsible use of Social Media as a recruitment tool Coordinate other assigned administrative tasks such as video, team travel, and equipment as assigned by the head coach QUALIFICATIONS  Any combination of education and experience that provides the required knowledge, skills, and abilities to perform the duties of this position A demonstrated commitment to inclusion, equity, and social justice with experience providing support and advocacy for historically marginalized groups. Experience with Word, Excel, Powerpoint, Hudl, and ARMS. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Superior time management and organizational skills. Ability to set priorities and meet deadlines. Knowledge of and adherence to University policies, particularly as they apply to student safety and hazing. Must be able to successfully articulate the values of a liberal arts education and the role intercollegiate athletics plays in the development of student-athletes. Ability to effectively interact with a wide variety of people in a manner that positively portrays the University and its programs, personnel, and philosophies. Thorough knowledge of and adherence to all applicable NCAA Div. III and Conference rules as they apply to the activities and programs within the incumbent's designated sport.  Previous coaching or high-level playing experience preferred Typical Work Schedule Tuesday through Friday, 4 - 7 pm Weekend work is common during the season This position is 9-month, 20 hours a week. Physical Demands & Working Conditions: Typical work is outdoors. Physical effort is common and involves lifting up to 50 pounds. Salary: $15.55/hr You will need to upload the following two documents as part of your application materials in the \"My Experience\" section labeled Resume: Brief cover letter addressing the qualifications Current Resume Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. ​ Incomplete applications will not be considered. BACKGROUND CHECK REQUIREMENT: All University positions require that candidates submit to a criminal conviction record check prior to hire. Conviction does not automatically preclude candidates from being hired. Nature of conviction will be considered relative to the duties of the position.   REASONABLE ACCOMMODATIONS STATEMENT: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. INSTRUCTIONS FOR APPLICANTS: Please read the following carefully before beginning the online application process. To be considered for employment at Willamette University, please complete our online employment application. Your application and all required attachments -- listed at the bottom of the page -- must be submitted for each individual job post that you are interested in applying. Once you submit your application you will not be able to edit your application."
    },
    "https://willamette.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Salem-Campus/Maintenance-Repair-Worker-III---HVAC_R0007119": {
      "title": "Maintenance Repair Worker III / HVAC",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT WILLAMETTE UNIVERSITY: Willamette University , founded in 1842, is a nationally-renowned private university enrolling 2800 students across five colleges. Our historic campus, adjacent to the Oregon State Capitol, hosts a distinguished undergraduate liberal arts college in Salem, Oregon. Our downtown Portland campus is home to the Pacific Northwest College of Art (PNCA). We offer a wide range of professional graduate programs, including Oregon’s top-ranked MBA program , the Northwest’s oldest law school, as well as MA/MFA programs at PNCA and master’s degrees in data science and computer science. Willamette University provides a high-value and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our Benefits Summary includes options for health, dental, life insurance, retirement, substantial paid time off, tuition and more. If you need assistance applying for a job or have any questions on recruitment at Willamette, please contact our HR Department , hr@willamette.edu or call us at 503-370-6210. POSITION SUMMARY The Facilities Department at Willamette University is responsible for the daily operations, maintenance and upkeep of approximately 1.4 million square feet of academic, residential, administrative and off campus properties situated on approximately 60 acres with all the associated utilities and infrastructure. Under general direction, the Maintenance Repair Worker III performs advanced skilled maintenance, repair, troubleshooting, and operational support for university buildings, systems, and infrastructure. This position works independently on complex maintenance tasks and serves as a senior-level technician supporting campus operations, life safety systems, and preventative maintenance programs. The technician is responsible for maintaining a safe, functional, and reliable campus environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. This is the senior/specialist worker level of the Maintenance Repair Worker series.   RESPONSIBILITIES Practices and encourages Facilities Management workplace expectations.  Is familiar with state boiler laws and CSD-1 Inspect, adjust, maintain and repair facilities operating systems, such as Mechanical, plumbing and electrical systems, kitchen equipment and pumps/pumping systems. Troubleshoot and repair building DDC and pneumatic control system. Maintain and repair control air compressor system to include but not limited to: Tear down and overhaul of compressor and motors. Operates, maintains and repairs boiler room equipment in accordance with good engineering standards, State laws, and safe work practices. Ensure that all preventive maintenance is  accomplished as prescribed by the State of Oregon, owner’s insurance company and  manufacturer’s requirements Coordinate boiler repair, maintenance and upgrades with contractors to include requesting, reviewing and proper close out of contracted work. Performs preventative maintenance tasks such as changing filters, cleaning and lubrication of operating equipment, cleaning coils, belt changing and alignment, sheaves changes and bearing replacements. Assists in the coordination of the preventive maintenance program through scheduled inspections, equipment service, and maintaining records of repairs and maintenance performed.  Accompanies and assists ITM contractors and inspectors. Diagnose equipment failures and determine corrective actions Maintains an inventory of critical spare parts, supplies, and equipment. May coordinate the work of semiskilled assistants or other helpers such as trades/maintenance workers, laborers or students. Support campus emergencies, severe weather response, and after-hours callouts Subject to after hour’s callback for emergencies.  Assists other team members as needed.  Performs other maintenance related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS Minimum High School Diploma and Five years of progressively responsible facility maintenance experience Minimum of five years experience as a Maintenance Repair Worker involving skilled work related to the maintenance and repair of buildings and related equipment required OR completion of an approved Mechanical Maintenance Apprenticeship Program. Basic computer skills such as typing, email and the ability to fill out and complete time sheets and service request forms online required. Possession of a valid Oregon driver’s license and a satisfactory driving record or the ability to obtain one within 60 days of date of hire. Must have the ability to effectively interact with a variety of people in a manner that emphasizes strong customer service and portrays the University’s programs, personnel and philosophies in a positive manner.  Must have the ability to work independently as well as establish and maintain harmonious relations with other staff, faculty and students. Licenses or Certifications Limited Maintenance Electrician license or greater required. Abilities Organize and update computerized logs; Routinely and safely lifts 50 pounds.  Work while walking, stooping, bending over and/or standing for prolonged periods of time and while exposed to dirt, dust, infectious waste, obnoxious odors, and inclement weather;  Estimate time and materials;  Climb ladders and work in confined spaces;  Communicate both orally and in written English.  Have the knowledge and training in the safety hazards and precautions associate with this position and other building maintenance functions. Must have knowledge of and be able to use the appropriate PPE (Personal protective equipment) as needed. OTHER REQUIREMENTS Accountability: Ability to accept responsibility and account for actions. Customer Oriented: Ability to provide a high level of customer service while following company procedures. Detail Oriented: Ability to pay attention to the minute details of a project or task. Calm & Efficient: Ability to deal with emergencies in a calm and efficient manner. Organized: Possessing the trait of being organized or following a systematic method for tasks. Communication: Ability to communicate positively and effectively with a wide variety of clients in person, by phone, or in writing.   Typical Work Schedule: 7:30am – 4:00pm M-F Salary: $28.85 per hour (~$60,000 annually) You will need to upload the following two documents as part of your application materials in the \"My Experience\" section labeled Resume: Cover letter addressing qualifications Current resume Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. ​Incomplete applications will not be considered. BACKGROUND CHECK REQUIREMENT: All University positions require that candidates submit to a criminal conviction record check prior to hire. Conviction does not automatically preclude candidates from being hired. Nature of conviction will be considered relative to the duties of the position.   REASONABLE ACCOMMODATIONS STATEMENT: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. INSTRUCTIONS FOR APPLICANTS: Please read the following carefully before beginning the online application process. To be considered for employment at Willamette University, please complete our online employment application. Your application and all required attachments -- listed at the bottom of the page -- must be submitted for each individual job post that you are interested in applying. Once you submit your application you will not be able to edit your application."
    },
    "https://willamette.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Salem-Campus/Electrician_R0007093": {
      "title": "Electrician",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT WILLAMETTE UNIVERSITY: Willamette University , founded in 1842, is a nationally-renowned private university enrolling 2800 students across five colleges. Our historic campus, adjacent to the Oregon State Capitol, hosts a distinguished undergraduate liberal arts college in Salem, Oregon. Our downtown Portland campus is home to the Pacific Northwest College of Art (PNCA). We offer a wide range of professional graduate programs, including Oregon’s top-ranked MBA program , the Northwest’s oldest law school, as well as MA/MFA programs at PNCA and master’s degrees in data science and computer science. Willamette University provides a high-value and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our Benefits Summary includes options for health, dental, life insurance, retirement, substantial paid time off, tuition and more. If you need assistance applying for a job or have any questions on recruitment at Willamette, please contact our HR Department , hr@willamette.edu or call us at 503-370-6210. POSITION SUMMARY The Facilities Department at Willamette University is responsible for the daily operations, maintenance and upkeep of approximately 1.4 million square feet of academic, residential, administrative and off campus properties situated on approximately 60 acres with all the associated utilities and infrastructure. The Facilities Electrician is responsible for maintaining, repairing, and upgrading the electrical systems that support Willamette University’s academic, residential, and administrative buildings. This position ensures safe, reliable operation of campus electrical infrastructure while providing exceptional customer service to students, faculty, and staff. The electrician plays a crucial role in the day-to-day functioning of campus buildings and supports the University’s mission by creating a safe, comfortable, and energy-efficient environment. RESPONSIBILITIES Electrical Maintenance & Repair Perform skilled work in the installation, alteration, maintenance and repair of the University electrical systems, equipment and fixtures in accordance with standard practices of the trade. Diagnose and resolve issues involving fire alarm systems, lighting systems, wiring, panels, breakers, motors, pumps, and building electrical components. Respond to daily service requests and prioritize work to minimize disruption to campus operations. Installation & System Upgrades Install, modify and maintain electrical systems, including circuits, conduit, lighting, controls, panels, motors, generators and related equipment. Support construction, renovation, and energy-efficiency projects in coordination with Facilities staff and contractors. Ensure all installations meet applicable electrical codes and University standards. Review blueprints and contractors’ work for deviation from code and specifications and report issues to Facilities Managers. Preventive Maintenance Conduct routine inspections and preventive maintenance on electrical panels, emergency lighting, generators, and specialized equipment. Track and document all maintenance activities and repairs in the University’s work order system. Identify opportunities to improve system reliability and reduce operational downtime. Safety & Compliance Advise Facilities Managers on all code discrepancies and deviations to plans. Perform all work in compliance with NEC, Oregon Electrical Code, OSHA regulations, and University safety policies. Follow proper Lockout/Tagout (LOTO), fall protection, and confined space procedures. Actively promote a safe working environment and report hazardous conditions. Operational & Customer Support Collaborate with HVAC, Plumbing, Carpentry, and other Facilities teams to support building operations. Provide clear, professional communication to faculty, staff, and students regarding project timelines and service impacts. Assist with campus events and special operational needs requiring electrical support. Emergency Response Respond promptly to after-hours emergencies such as electrical outages and critical system failures. Assist in restoring power and equipment functionality quickly and safely. Respond to fire alarms and other emergencies. Documentation & Inventory Management Maintain accurate records of repairs, upgrades, and system changes, including panel schedules and equipment labeling. General Manages and encourages Facilities Management workplace expectations, valuing all persons and treating everyone with dignity and respect. Fills in on weekends and holidays when required. Subject to after-hours call backs. Performs other duties as assigned. OTHER REQUIREMENTS Accountability: Ability to accept responsibility and account for actions. Customer Oriented: Ability to provide a high level of customer service while following company procedures. Detail Oriented: Ability to pay attention to the minute details of a project or task. Calm & Efficient: Ability to deal with emergencies in a calm and efficient manner. Organized: Possessing the trait of being organized or following a systematic method for tasks. Communication: Ability to communicate positively and effectively with a wide variety of clients in person, by phone, or in writing.   QUALIFICATIONS Minimum Any combination of education and experience that provides the required knowledge, skills and abilities to perform the essential functions of the position. High school education with some college coursework preferred. Oregon Limited Maintenance Electrician (LME) License, General Journeyman Electrician (J) License, or an equivalent state-recognized electrical license. Three years of experience performing electrical maintenance, installation, troubleshooting, and repair in commercial, institutional, or industrial facilities. Demonstrated knowledge of: Electrical codes, standards, and safety regulations (including NEC); low-voltage and line-voltage systems; and electrical distribution systems, controls, and motor equipment. Proficient use of a personal computer and software programs such as Word, Excel and any other specialized applications required. Keyboarding, email and maintaining databases required. Willingness and ability to quickly learn new computer skills. Possess a thorough knowledge of building construction, maintenance and custodial/housekeeping related trades and be familiar with Maintenance terminology/operations. Excellent organizational skills and ability to manage competing priorities in order to meet deadlines. Ability to work in a fast-paced team oriented environment. Must possess an understanding of accounting processes and mathematics. Must be able to buy selectively through the competitive bidding process. Able to estimate time and materials accurately. Requires considerable contact with individuals outside the University and a high level of contact with individuals within the University, and requires the interpersonal skills necessary for such contact. Experience with record keeping and file maintenance skills to keep accurate records of purchases, purchase orders issued, payments, warranty information, and vendor lists. Must have the ability to effectively interact with a variety of people in a manner that emphasizes strong customer service and portrays the University’s programs, personnel, and philosophies in a positive manner. Knowledge of safety hazards and precautions related to building and equipment maintenance such as OSHA, Hazardous Communications, DEQ, and EPA regulations. Ability to work independently as well as establish and maintain harmonious relations with other staff, faculty and students. Must possess a valid Oregon driver’s license and have a satisfactory driving record in order to drive university vehicles and carts. Preferred State of Oregon General Journeyman Electrician License (J-level) or equivalent out-of-state licensure with ability to obtain Oregon reciprocity. State of Oregon General Supervising Electrician License, Limited Supervising Manufacturing Plant Electrician License, General Journeyman License or Limited Journeyman Manufacturing Plant Electrician License required. Five+ years of experience performing electrical maintenance, troubleshooting, and installation in a commercial, industrial, or institutional setting—preferably within higher education or public facilities. Demonstrated experience with Building Automation Systems (BAS), including controls troubleshooting and integration with HVAC systems. Experience with energy-efficient technologies, LED retrofits, motor controls, VFDs, and power-quality troubleshooting. Strong proficiency with CMMS work order systems (e.g., TMA, FAMIS, AiM, SchoolDude). Working knowledge of NFPA 70E, NEC, OSHA regulations, and industry safety best practices. Experience with low-voltage systems, including fire alarms, access control, CCTV, and data/communication systems. Demonstrated ability to work effectively in occupied academic buildings, coordinating work with students, faculty, and staff with minimal disruption. Typical Work Schedule: 7:30am – 4:00pm M-F Salary: $38.46 per hour (~$80,000 annually) You will need to upload the following two documents as part of your application materials in the \"My Experience\" section labeled Resume: Cover letter addressing qualifications Current resume Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. ​Incomplete applications will not be considered. BACKGROUND CHECK REQUIREMENT: All University positions require that candidates submit to a criminal conviction record check prior to hire. Conviction does not automatically preclude candidates from being hired. Nature of conviction will be considered relative to the duties of the position.   REASONABLE ACCOMMODATIONS STATEMENT: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. INSTRUCTIONS FOR APPLICANTS: Please read the following carefully before beginning the online application process. To be considered for employment at Willamette University, please complete our online employment application. Your application and all required attachments -- listed at the bottom of the page -- must be submitted for each individual job post that you are interested in applying. Once you submit your application you will not be able to edit your application."
    },
    "https://willamette.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Salem-Campus/Facilities-Management-Purchaser_R0007089": {
      "title": "Facilities Management Purchaser",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-26\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT WILLAMETTE UNIVERSITY: Willamette University , founded in 1842, is a nationally-renowned private university enrolling 2800 students across five colleges. Our historic campus, adjacent to the Oregon State Capitol, hosts a distinguished undergraduate liberal arts college in Salem, Oregon. Our downtown Portland campus is home to the Pacific Northwest College of Art (PNCA). We offer a wide range of professional graduate programs, including Oregon’s top-ranked MBA program , the Northwest’s oldest law school, as well as MA/MFA programs at PNCA and master’s degrees in data science and computer science. Willamette University provides a high-value and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our Benefits Summary includes options for health, dental, life insurance, retirement, substantial paid time off, tuition and more. If you need assistance applying for a job or have any questions on recruitment at Willamette, please contact our HR Department , hr@willamette.edu or call us at 503-370-6210. POSITION SUMMARY The Facilities Department at Willamette University is responsible for the daily operations, maintenance and upkeep of approximately 1.4 million square feet of academic, residential, administrative and off campus properties situated on approximately 60 acres with all the associated utilities and infrastructure. The Facilities Management Purchaser provides centralized purchasing in support of all Facilities departments. Daily duties will primarily involve the procurement, purchasing and issuing of parts and supplies for the Facilities Maintenance team. This position also receives and distributes freight deliveries, issues and reconciles P numbers, reconciles P-Card purchase records, prices out and completes work orders. Updates and maintains all Facilities SDS and equipment warranty records. Serves as backup to Facilities office staff as required. RESPONSIBILITIES Manages and encourages Facilities Management workplace expectations, valuing all persons and treating everyone with dignity and respect. Interacts in a professional manner with suppliers on a day to day basis. Responsible for sourcing and purchasing parts and materials for all Facilities departments at the best value to the University. Procures and arranges for the pickup or delivery of all parts, materials, and supplies used by Facilities departments on a daily, routine or ongoing basis. Procures and arranges for the pick up or delivery of parts, materials, furnishings and supplies for routine, special or emergency projects. Verifies and tracks received inventory and completes inventory reports and logs. Reconciles shipping invoices and receiving reports to ensure count accuracy. Receives, unloads, and processes deliveries. Refuses acceptance of damaged, unacceptable, or incorrect items. Troubleshoots vendor delivery issues and oversees the return process. Maintains accurate purchasing records. Issues P numbers and reconciles the P number log. Maintains records and files for effective, accurate tracking of maintenance and repairs, ensuring proper coding and monitoring of all cost and quality factors. Responsible for updating prices and materials in the Asset Planner Service Request system. Maintains price lists and price agreements. May write bids and specifications as needed. Is responsible for acquiring and keeping updated records of all SDS documents that pertain to Facilities purchases and for directing the SDS documents to the appropriate departmental personnel. Issues parts and materials as required. Maintains the security of parts and materials under the purchaser’s control. Serves in a backup role for the various Facilities office staff as needed. May supervise a work study student in the picking-up and delivery of parts. If workload permits, performs other Facilities maintenance related duties as required. Subject to after-hours call backs. Performs other duties as assigned. OTHER REQUIREMENTS Accountability: Ability to accept responsibility and account for actions. Customer Oriented: Ability to provide a high level of customer service while following company procedures. Detail Oriented: Ability to pay attention to the minute details of a project or task. Calm & Efficient: Ability to deal with emergencies in a calm and efficient manner. Organized: Possessing the trait of being organized or following a systematic method for tasks. Communication: Ability to communicate positively and effectively with a wide variety of clients in person, by phone, or in writing. QUALIFICATIONS Minimum Any combination of education and experience that provides the required knowledge, skills and abilities to perform the essential functions of the position. High school education with some college coursework preferred. Two years of related work experience in building construction, maintenance and custodial/housekeeping or related trades in addition to a minimum of two years’ of experience in purchasing and supplying parts and materials: or equivalent experience in order to successfully perform the duties of the job. Proficient use of a personal computer and software programs such as Word, Excel and any other specialized applications required. Keyboarding, email and maintaining databases required. Willingness and ability to quickly learn new computer skills. Possess a thorough knowledge of building construction, maintenance and custodial/housekeeping related trades and be familiar with Maintenance terminology/operations. Excellent organizational skills and ability to manage competing priorities in order to meet deadlines. Ability to work in a fast paced team oriented environment. Must possess an understanding of accounting processes and mathematics. Must be able to buy selectively through the competitive bidding process. Able to estimate time and materials accurately. Requires considerable contact with individuals outside the University and a high level of contact with individuals within the University, and requires the interpersonal skills necessary for such contact. Experience with record keeping and file maintenance skills to keep accurate records of purchases, purchase orders issued, payments, warranty information, and vendor lists. Must have the ability to effectively interact with a variety of people in a manner that emphasizes strong customer service and portrays the University’s programs, personnel, and philosophies in a positive manner. Knowledge of safety hazards and precautions related to building and equipment maintenance such as OSHA, Hazardous Communications, DEQ, and EPA regulations. Ability to negotiate skillfully in tough situations with both internal and external customers. Have the ability to work independently as well as establish and maintain relations with other staff, faculty and students. Must possess a valid Oregon driver’s license and have a satisfactory driving record in order to drive university vehicles and carts. Preferred Experience in and the ability to become certified in driving a forklift College coursework relevant to the position Typical Work Schedule: 7:30am – 4:00pm M-F Salary: $24.52 per hour (~$51,000 annually) You will need to upload the following two documents as part of your application materials in the \"My Experience\" section labeled Resume: Cover letter addressing qualifications Current resume Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. ​Incomplete applications will not be considered. BACKGROUND CHECK REQUIREMENT: All University positions require that candidates submit to a criminal conviction record check prior to hire. Conviction does not automatically preclude candidates from being hired. Nature of conviction will be considered relative to the duties of the position.   REASONABLE ACCOMMODATIONS STATEMENT: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. INSTRUCTIONS FOR APPLICANTS: Please read the following carefully before beginning the online application process. To be considered for employment at Willamette University, please complete our online employment application. Your application and all required attachments -- listed at the bottom of the page -- must be submitted for each individual job post that you are interested in applying. Once you submit your application you will not be able to edit your application."
    }
